# Cloudflare Pages cache control.
#
# Earlier rules with `/styles/*` + `/scripts/*` + explicit
# `/styles/sections/*` failed silently — the CDN kept serving 4-hour
# cache headers, so a CSS deploy could sit invisible for hours. Switched
# to the simplest possible model: catch-all force-revalidate, then a
# single override for the only path that really should cache long.
#
# More specific paths win, so /assets/* still gets its long cache,
# /api/* (Pages Functions) is explicitly no-store.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, immutable

/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
